      "message": "fix(verify): the rapid law reads the stock's top under the rapid, not its highest point\n\nLaw (d) caps every column at the stock's highest point, so on a stepped\n\"from model\" or carried stock a Bore's entry dive to just above the low\npart was convicted as if the boss stood there too, and the post was\nblocked for a legal program.\n\nverify::acquit_by_stock_top re-reads an upright vertical dive the column\nlaw convicted (column modes only) against the stock and part solids\nunder the tool: the highest vertex of every facet whose plan comes\nwithin each stack band's disc - the flute at full radius from the tip,\nthe shank from the flute's top, the holder from the shank's top. It only\nremoves a conviction, and only where every band ends above that exact\nupper bound; non-finite input, no judged stock, or a flute disc meeting\nno facet leaves it standing. Wired at the upright and the 3+2 sites\n(local facets there), before acquit_by_prior.\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/stepped_stock_rapid.rs (part- and\nstock-sourced Bore: the dive over the low step passes and posts; the\nboss under it, or under the rim only, is convicted and blocks the post)\nand sim::verify::stock_top's unit tests.\n\nFixes #1091\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
