  {
    "sha": "6440858bcd6c69b7807ef3535bff77d8e82caa85",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDY0NDA4NThiY2Q2YzY5Yjc4MDdlZjM1MzViZmY3N2Q4ZTgyY2FhODU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-12T07:16:31Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-12T07:16:31Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(verify): the stock-top re-reading proves nothing from an open mesh\n\nPR #1098 review: acquit_by_stock_top's bound (\"the material over a plan\npoint stands under a facet covering it\") holds only for a closed\nsurface. A from-model stock whose boss lost its top facets let a\nstock-sourced Bore's rapid to Z 22 into a boss standing to Z 30 post.\n\nEvery solid the re-reading reads must now pass\nstock_top_shell::closed_shell or the conviction stands: non-empty,\nfinite, no 3-D degenerate facet, every undirected edge (exact endpoint\nmatch) used by exactly two facets once each way, one edge-connected\nshell, positive signed volume. Computed once per solid per operation,\nO(F) with an edge hash map.\n\nPinned by stepped_stock_rapid::an_open_stock_mesh_proves_nothing_and_\nthe_dive_stays_convicted (part- and stock-sourced Bore; fails with the\ngate off) and stock_top unit tests for an open shell, non-manifold and\nduplicated edges, degenerate, inside-out, split, empty and non-finite\nsolids.\n\nRefs #1091\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
